<article class="env-lemma" id="06CW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06CW">Lemma <span data-tag="06CW">97.5.2</span>.</a> Let $p : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ and $q : \mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ be $1$-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. If $p$ and $q$ are limit preserving on objects, then so is the composition $q \circ p$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is formal. Let $U = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{i \in I} U_ i$ be the directed limit of affine schemes $U_ i$ over $S$, let $z_ i$ be an object of $\mathcal{Z}$ over $U_ i$ for some $i$, let $x$ be an object of $\mathcal{X}$ over $U$, and let $\gamma : q(p(x)) \to z_ i|_ U$ be an isomorphism. As $q$ is limit preserving on objects there exist an $i' \geq i$, an object $y_{i'}$ of $\mathcal{Y}$ over $U_{i'}$, an isomorphism $\beta : y_{i'}|_ U \to p(x)$, and an isomorphism $\gamma _{i'} : q(y_{i'}) \to z_ i|_{U_{i'}}$ such that (<a href="/tag/06CU" data-tag="06CU">97.5.0.1</a>) is commutative. As $p$ is limit preserving on objects there exist an $i'' \geq i'$, an object $x_{i''}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over $U_{i''}$, an isomorphism $\beta ' : x_{i''}|_ U \to x$, and an isomorphism $\gamma '_{i''} : p(x_{i''}) \to y_{i'}|_{U_{i''}}$ such that (<a href="/tag/06CU" data-tag="06CU">97.5.0.1</a>) is commutative. The solution is to take $x_{i''}$ over $U_{i''}$ with isomorphism 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  q(p(x_{i''})) \xrightarrow {q(\gamma '_{i''})} q(y_{i'})|_{U_{i''}} \xrightarrow {\gamma _{i'}|_{U_{i''}}} z_ i|_{U_{i''}}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       and isomorphism $\beta ' : x_{i''}|_ U \to x$. We omit the verification that (<a href="/tag/06CU" data-tag="06CU">97.5.0.1</a>) is commutative. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>